.TH HOSTNAMEFETCH 1 "2026-11-24" "hostnamefetch 2026.11.24.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hostnamefetch \- neofetch-style system information with a hostname banner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hostnamefetch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hostnamefetch
prints system information next to a five-line banner rendered from the
local hostname.
.PP
It is a single Bash script and does not require a build step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.B \-\-stdout
Print the report instead of drawing it interactively.
.TP
.BI \-\-banner " on|off"
Enable or disable the hostname banner.
.TP
.BI \-\-banner_text " TEXT"
Render a custom banner instead of the local hostname.
.TP
.BI \-\-banner_chars " CHARSET"
Select the banner character set.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " MODE"
Select the layout mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-disable " ITEM"
Disable an information item.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/os-release
Distribution information.
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/WispW/hostnamefetch
